## Choosing Exciting Technologies

The Choose Boring Technology manifesto opposes early adoption and can slow down innovation.

Choosing a framework, technology or language can make us slower at delivering value. It can make it harder to maintain the codebase in the future. Fewer developers know it. All of this matters from a short-term business perspective. But in life and work there is more to it than simply maximizing the business value of everything we do. It is important to keep the business in mind and optimize return on investment (ROI), but it is too easy to fall into the trap of over-optimizing.

This new and exciting thing will make our team learn much faster than something well established. It will bring a new perspective to what we already know. It can help attract talent. It can bring more joy to programming. Sometimes the business risk outweighs it all. Those, but it is rare. We tend to overestimate business risk.

Technology, especially niche technology, can be a good filter for hiring developers. If someone is interested in Elixir, we can assume they are curious, something essential for a programmer.

Don't follow general rules blindly. If excitement drives you, you are not alone. Join the _Choose Exciting Technology_ club.

Finally, according to the Stack Overflow survey. Elixir and Phoenix are among the most loved and best paid technologies in the market.

![Phoenix](phoenix.png)
![Phoenix 2](phoenix2.png)

## Summary

Why choose Elixir and Phoenix?

- Technical Reason: The Erlang VM (Beam) has more than 30 years of evolution in distributed and concurrent environments, which makes it ideal for today's systems.

- Business Reason: Using modern technologies like Elixir allows you to hire curious people, who are more likely to be good candidates. The reduction in dependencies will save costs in the medium and long term.

- Emotional Reason: Elixir and Phoenix are modern, easy-to-learn languages and frameworks, which makes them fun and helps motivate people to experiment and generate new ideas or solutions. They are also well valued in the market and job offers are well paid.

